"digest":"6faefae665a13ca0bbad831c3f770ad7a8097c1ac637f311cd6ea67ccf1a97fd"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T8","usage":{"input_tokens":59077,"output_tokens":2462,"requests":5}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"f483481cf54f7f7bd4028e92ee63545b80deffbe2bade9b673a46f268c174c57"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:project.symbol-reference-completeness","usage":{"input_tokens":143390,"output_tokens":2857,"requests":7}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State and test how the cache-ineffective warning behaves when a non-caching fallback leg serves a call in a chain whose primary caches, or record that case as a known, accepted limitation.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.net-mechanism","project.portability"],"criteria":["E3","E5"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["\"the fallback-chain merge carries `prompt_caching` from the primary, as it does `prompt_cache_style`\"","Title: 'Cache-ineffective warning fires on Bedrock vendors that have no prompt caching'","The only chain test checks that the field is copied, not how the warning behaves when the fallback serves"],"finding":"Taking prompt_caching from the primary in the fallback-chain merge leaves the bug in place when a caching primary falls back to a non-caching Bedrock vendor. With anthropic primary and qwen fallback, cache settings are still sent and caching_requested=True. If the qwen leg serves the call, pydantic-ai drops the cache points, both counters are 0, and the cache-ineffective warning still fires although caching was never possible.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f1bf02dba20187796","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 2 (src/rebar/llm/runner_support.py) / Testing: 'The chain merge takes prompt_caching from the primary.'","norm_id":"nd602c5d0a4152510","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Chain [anthropic Bedrock primary, qwen Bedrock fallback]: the primary is throttled, qwen serves above the floor, the counters are 0, and a false 'NO effect' warning is logged"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Acknowledge, and either accept with a rationale or prevent, the loss of prompt caching for a caching Bedrock fallback behind a non-caching primary, and qualify the claim that a caching model's settings are unchanged.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.net-mechanism","project.portability"],"criteria":["E3"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["\"`cache_settings_for` returns `None` for the `bedrock` style when `prompt_caching` is False\"","\"the fallback-chain merge carries `prompt_caching` from the primary\"","\"A caching model's settings are unchanged.\" (true only for single-model use, not for a caching fallback behind a non-caching primary)"],"finding":"The plan changes existing behavior for a chain with a non-caching primary and a caching fallback without acknowledging it. Today a [qwen, anthropic] Bedrock chain gets bedrock cache settings, which pydantic-ai applies when the anthropic leg serves. After the fix, cache_settings_for returns None for the merged chain because prompt_caching follows the primary. The anthropic fallback then loses prompt caching, a silent cost and latency regression.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc608cf7c383cbfbe","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 1 (cache_settings_for returns None when prompt_caching is False) combined with step 2 (merge takes prompt_caching from the primary)","norm_id":"n21ff5e93780fa4b7","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Chain [qwen primary, anthropic fallback]: qwen fails over, anthropic serves with no cachePoint, and caching that worked before the fix is lost"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Decide how the chain-fallback path is handled: either set caching_requested from the answering candidate's `prompt_caching` (look up ran_model among the per-candidate caps) and add a test where a caching primary falls back to a non-caching candidate, or state explicitly that this residual false warning on a mixed-vendor fallback is out of scope.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.6,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: \"the fallback-chain merge carries `prompt_caching` from the primary, as it does `prompt_cache_style`\"","runner_support.py:76 `prompt_cache_style=per_candidate[0].prompt_cache_style` — the merge follows the primary","runner.py:603-604 `caching_requested=cache_settings is not None, model=ran_model` — the warning names the model that answered, which can be a fallback","runner_support.py:70-71 already accepts that 'a rare fallback runs uncached-but-correct', but nothing stops the false warning on that path"],"finding":"In a fallback chain, prompt_caching follows the primary, but the warning is reported against the model that actually answered. When a caching primary (e.g. Bedrock Claude) fails over to a non-caching Bedrock candidate (e.g. qwen), cache settings are still sent, the candidate ignores them, both counters are 0, and the 'prompt caching requested ... but had NO effect' warning fires for a model that could never cache. That is the same false positive this plan sets out to remove. The plan neither handles this path nor marks it out of scope.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa37e6ab544ed5fc8","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 2 (src/rebar/llm/runner_support.py chain merge) / src/rebar/llm/runner.py:601-604","norm_id":"n9eca22534407379e","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A chain of us.anthropic.claude-* with a qwen/mistral Bedrock fallback; the primary is throttled, qwen answers with input above the floor, and the cache-ineffective warning names qwen"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.6667,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add an assertion in test_bedrock_cache_capability.py that `structured.native_output_stack_supported` returns the same value before and after the fix for a qwen Bedrock id, given the same botocore outputConfig availability.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["E1","E6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.8243,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC3: 'Non-caching Bedrock models keep `prompt_cache_style=\"bedrock\"`, so native structured-output routing is unchanged, shown by a test.'","Testing: '`prompt_caching` is False, `prompt_cache_style` stays `bedrock`' — no assertion on native_output_stack_supported"],"finding":"AC3 promises that 'native structured-output routing is unchanged, shown by a test', but the new test only asserts that `prompt_cache_style` stays `bedrock`. Nothing asserts the routing outcome itself, i.e. what `structured.native_output_stack_supported` returns for a non-caching, native-output vendor such as qwen.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ffe71ab2211779a65","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance criteria AC3 / Testing first bullet","norm_id":"n70aea179e821b818","priority":0.1257,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A later refactor makes native_output_stack_supported read prompt_caching (or cache_settings_for). qwen, google, minimax or nvidia then silently lose native output, yet the prompt_cache_style assertion still passes."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"In the new test file, for qwen (and optionally nvidia), assert `native_output_stack_supported(capabilities)` is True when the botocore outputConfig check passes, alongside the prompt_cache_style assertion.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2857,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State which execution mode(s) the end-to-end PydanticAIRunner test covers; by default, parametrize the qwen and anthropic end-to-end cases over both modes.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["E2","E6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.49,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Testing: '`cache_settings_for` returns None in both execution modes'","Testing: 'End to end through `PydanticAIRunner` ... a qwen run ... logs no cache-ineffective warning, and the request carries no `cachePoint`' — mode unspecified"],"finding":"The unit test checks `cache_settings_for` 'in both execution modes', but the end-to-end PydanticAIRunner test does not say which execution mode it runs. If the other mode (e.g. the agentic message-cache path covered by test_agentic_message_cache.py) builds requests or `caching_requested` differently, that mode's warning and cachePoint behavior goes unproven.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f67e0b148d2f6d980","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Testing — end-to-end bullet","norm_id":"n98dbdfc6792722e1","priority":0.11,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The executor writes the end-to-end test only for the structured mode, while the agentic mode still marks messages with cache points or sets caching_requested by another route."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Parametrize the qwen no-warning/no-cachePoint case and the anthropic still-warns case over both execution modes used in the unit test.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify that the commit SHA, the exit code (0) and a UTC timestamp of the `make verify` run are recorded as a ticket comment when the AC is checked.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["E6","F1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.6,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'[non-codebase] `env -u JIRA_URL -u JIRA_USER -u JIRA_API_TOKEN make verify` exits 0 on the commit pushed for review.'","provenance: 'instrument=live-call — exit status and log live outside the repository'"],"finding":"The [non-codebase] `make verify` AC places its evidence outside the repository but does not say what concrete attestation will be recorded on the ticket. The provenance gives only 'exit status and log live outside the repository'; it names no commit SHA, exit code or timestamp to record.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f029af32f282b8fd7","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance criteria — [non-codebase] make verify line","norm_id":"n8a9ddf0d59218729","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reviewer cannot confirm which commit the verify run covered, or whether it ran after the final push."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Append to the AC: 'attestation recorded on the ticket: commit SHA, exit code 0, UTC timestamp of the run'.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.1429,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails